{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nAfter bug 84c7 removed the four ghost rows, **all 9 remaining `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` rows\ndeclare an empty prefix**. `_rebar_env: (0, \"REBAR_\")` was the only row that ever used the\nsecond tuple element, and its helper was drained out of the tree by the RP-04 cutover\n(`d361eb28e4`).\n\nThe prefix is still applied at `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` `_scan_call`\n(`reads.setdefault(prefix + lit, ...)`) and at `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`\n`_helper_access` (`return self._resolved_env(node, prefix + lit)`).\n\n## Why it matters\nThe feature has **zero production users and zero live end-to-end coverage**, and its only\nhistorical coverage passed for the wrong reason (see the 84c7 comment correction). An\nunused-but-wired feature in two CI gate scripts is a maintenance hazard: it cannot rot\nvisibly, only silently.\n\n## Decision (operator ruling, recorded in comments)\n**Remove the prefix field from both consumers**, simplifying both tables to a bare int\n(`helper name -> 0-indexed position of the env-name argument`). Rationale: no live row uses\na prefix, the 84c7-era held-out assertion is vacuous with every live prefix empty, and repo\npolicy prefers deleting unused code over testing an unused feature. A future prefixed\nhelper can re-add the field together with real coverage.\n\nScope:\n- `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`: `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` becomes `dict[str, int]`; `_scan_call`\n  stops applying a prefix.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`: `_helper_access` stops applying a prefix.\n- Tests touching the tuple shape updated (`test_known_env_helper_call_resolves_and_fires`\n  destructuring, the ghost-row literal in `test_gen_env_registry.py`).\n- `docs/env-vars.md` regenerates byte-identical (no live row used a prefix).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The prefix field is removed from `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` in both consumers and the\n      `prefix + lit` application code is gone from `_scan_call` and `_helper_access`.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` stay green.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is unchanged by the work (no live row uses a prefix).\n\n## Provenance\nObserved while fixing bug 84c7 (surprised-convincing-gopher); recorded rather than repaired\nthere. The remove-vs-cover design fork was escalated and resolved by operator ruling —\nsee comments."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787345736943202001,"uuid":"3d4d7571-74f4-40bb-a34d-afe6a3c13d5f"}